afk: pure refactor — extract isolated-task VCS operations behind a
VcsHandle interface (src/task/vcs.ts, GitCheckoutHandle).

Motivation: preparation for omp-jj-workspace-handle.patch, which adds a
second implementation (JjWorkspaceHandle) for pure jj workspaces. No
behavior change; git code paths move behind the interface unchanged.

What must survive a rebase:
- Only the seam matters: baseline capture, commit-to-ref, merge,
  cleanup, ref rescue, and patch apply go through a VcsHandle so a jj
  implementation can slot in. If upstream refactors these functions,
  re-cut the seam at the equivalent points; behavior must remain
  byte-identical for git repos.
- Apply order: this patch precedes omp-jj-workspace-handle.patch.
- Since 18.0.11 the old TS git façade (utils/git.ts) is gone;
  GitCheckoutHandle delegates to worktree.ts plus the native
  @oh-my-pi/pi-natives/vcs layer (canApplyPatch/applyPatch on
  VcsGitRepo). 18.x's rescueTaskBranch (#8868) moved into the handle as
  rescueTaskRef with identical semantics. New 18.x consumers of
  IsolationContext (security remediation, eval agent-bridge budget test)
  carry the vcs field in their mocked contexts.

Rebased 18.1.13 -> 18.2.10: isolation-runner grew a kept-alive release
path (releaseIsolation: capture + commitToTaskRef on lifecycle release),
retained-workspace handling and templated error/summary rendering; the
seam now routes those new call sites through the handle too. Upstream
pruned test/task/isolation-runner.test.ts, so this patch no longer edits
it; task-spawn.test.ts's mocked IsolationContext carries the vcs field.
NestedRepoPatch is imported from @oh-my-pi/pi-tui/tools/task.

Rebased 18.2.10 -> 18.6.0: upstream dropped the baseline from
IsolationContext (now `{ repoRoot }`) and captures each spawn's baseline
from its fresh isolation copy (captureIsolationBaseline) so parent drift
never shows up as task changes. The handle's captureBaseline() became
captureIsolationBaseline(isolationDir); IsolationContext is
`{ vcs, repoRoot }`. CommitToBranchResult now carries rootPatch (the
release path fingerprints it). New VcsHandle.assertMergeTarget(): upstream
resolves the git repo OUTSIDE mergeIsolatedChanges' try, so a vanished
checkout throws out of the merge phase (test/task/failed-child-artifact
depends on it); the seam calls it first to stay byte-identical.
security/remediation no longer consumes IsolationContext (it has its own
SecurityRemediationContext), so that test hunk is retired; the new
isolation-release.test.ts carries the vcs field.

